med, on their fingers. He tried to turn a deaf ear to these discussions of the best patterns of long clothes for the coming baby; tried to turn away and avoid seeing the mysterious, endless strips of knitting, the triangles of linen, and so on, to which Charissa attached special importance.\n <Assistant> I have read the book excerpt and I will answer the question you ask."